  "notes": "TRANSITIVITY:\n{他動詞|たどうし} (transitive)\nPair: {浸|ひた}る (intransitive - to be soaked)\nPattern: XをYに{浸|ひた}す\n\nASPECT (ている):\n{浸|ひた}している indicates ongoing action or resulting state (something is being/remaining soaked).\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- {水|みず}に{浸|ひた}す - to soak in water\n- お{湯|ゆ}に{浸|ひた}す - to soak in hot water\n- {出汁|だし}に{浸|ひた}す - to soak in broth\n\nCOOKING USAGE:\nUsed for rehydrating dried ingredients ({乾物|かんぶつ}), marinating, or preparing ingredients before cooking.\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- {浸|ひた}し{物|もの} / お{浸|ひた}し - boiled greens soaked in dashi\n- {水|みず}に{浸|ひた}しておく - to leave soaking in water",
